# Regression: a `style {` inside a string interpolation pushed a style frame on top of the
# string's frames, so the line terminator no longer ended the string (grammar.md §4.2) and
# the rest of the file was lexed in style mode (`let` became an `Ident`). A line terminator
# inside a string ends every frame from the string's frame upward, style frames included.
LetKw "let"
Ident "a"
Eq "="
StringStart "\""
InterpStart "{"
StyleKw "style"
LBrace "{"
Newline "\n"
LetKw "let"
Ident "b"
Eq "="
IntLit "1"
Newline "\n"
